import SwiftUI

struct PrivacyPolicyView: View {
    var body: some View {
        LegalArticleView(title: "Privacy Policy", intro: "Your stories, conversations and memories start on your device. This policy explains what Tideverse stores locally, what optional online AI requests share, and how you control your information.", sections: [
            ("1. Information stored on this device", "Conversations, selected photo attachments, authored story progress, story moments and user-approved memory notes are stored using SwiftData on your device. Unsent text drafts are stored separately in protected local files. Introduction completion, EULA acceptance version and date, settings and AI consent are stored in local app preferences, including the accepted notice version and the most recent acceptance and revocation dates. A materially updated notice requires your agreement again. No account is required for offline stories."),
            ("2. Optional AI requests", "If you explicitly agree and choose to send a message, the app sends your message, up to twelve recent conversation turns, current chapter and up to twelve validated story choices, up to twelve pinned memory notes, and any selected photo directly to DeepSeek over HTTPS using deepseek-flash. The provider also receives the network information needed to serve the request, such as your IP address."),
            ("3. International processing", "DeepSeek requests may be processed in mainland China, outside your country of residence. Do not send personal information you do not wish to transmit to an external provider."),
            ("4. Model-side storage", "DeepSeek may retain requests, responses and service logs under its applicable API terms and account settings. Tideverse does not promise that requests are never stored or used by the provider. Turning off AI permission prevents new requests; it does not delete information already processed by a provider."),
            ("5. Photos and device permissions", "Photos are selected through Apple's system Photos Picker. They are re-encoded to reduce size and remove embedded metadata before sending. Optional image text recognition runs locally only after you choose Read text."),
            ("6. Advertising and tracking", "Tideverse does not include advertising, social login, third-party analytics SDKs or cross-app tracking. You do not need to create an account to read stories or save progress."),
            ("7. User controls", "You can revoke consent for future AI requests in Settings, unpin or delete memory notes, delete local records and unsent drafts, and export or import a JSON archive. Unsent drafts are not included in archives. Deleting local content clears AI consent but retains introduction completion and EULA acceptance preferences; uninstalling the app removes these device preferences. You can exclude attached photos when exporting an archive; doing so does not delete them from this device. Removing a memory note does not remove the same information from conversation messages you keep; delete those messages or the conversation to exclude that text from future chat history. Deleting local content does not retroactively remove any data already processed by an external provider."),
            ("8. Security", "The app connects directly to DeepSeek using HTTPS. Selected photos are re-encoded before transmission to remove embedded metadata. Avoid including passwords, identity documents or other sensitive information in messages, photos and feedback reports."),
            ("9. Children", "All illustrated characters are fictional adults aged 25 or older. Tideverse does not ask children to provide personal information. Check the age rating in the App Store listing and use the device’s parental controls to manage access."),
            ("10. Changes and contact", "You can reopen this policy from Settings at any time. A changed AI data notice requires fresh permission before new online requests. For privacy questions, open Feedback & Suggestions and prepare a report without including sensitive information. Any published support and privacy-policy links are available in Developer Information.")
        ])
    }
}
